# 🧱 System Architecture

```txt id="kg5vlt"
React Frontend
      ↓
REST API Request
      ↓
Node.js + Express Backend
      ↓
SQL Database
```

---

# 📌 Architecture Overview

## 1️⃣ React Frontend

React handles all frontend user interfaces, including:

* Homepage
* Treatment Listing Page
* Treatment Detail Page
* Booking Form
* Enquiry Form
* Admin Dashboard UI

Users will browse treatments, submit enquiries, make bookings, and process payments through the React frontend.

---

## 2️⃣ REST API Request

The frontend communicates with the backend through REST API requests.

Example endpoints:

```txt id="0bxhgh"
GET    /api/services
GET    /api/services/:id
POST   /api/bookings
POST   /api/enquiries
POST   /api/payments
```

---

## 3️⃣ Node.js + Express Backend

The backend handles application logic, including:

* Treatment management
* Customer enquiry handling
* Booking processing
* Payment record management
* Admin authentication
* Database connectivity

---

## 4️⃣ SQL Database

The database stores:

* Treatment information
* Customer enquiries
* Booking records
* Payment status
* Admin account data
* Website content data

---

# 🔐 Authentication Architecture

The admin system uses JWT-based authentication.

```txt id="moh2bx"
Admin Login
     ↓
JWT Token
     ↓
Protected Admin Routes
     ↓
Admin Dashboard
```

After login, administrators are able to:

* Create treatment services
* Update treatment content
* Delete services
* View booking records
* View enquiries

